WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:05.088
But what if we could stop an asteroid from
hitting in the first place?

00:00:05.585 --> 00:00:08.091
Some of our brightest minds think we can.

00:00:08.684 --> 00:00:09.426
How's that feel?

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:09.968
Good.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.139
This film is about the threat of asteroids

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:16.766
and what we can actually do about that.

00:00:17.735 --> 00:00:21.312
It seems such a perfect marriage, this subject with IMAX.

00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:23.982
It's exciting, it's educational.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.110
We show how scientists assess whether they're a threat,

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.110
what their orbits are,

00:00:28.691 --> 00:00:30.155
what affects their orbits.

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:33.199
And then, if they are a threat, how we can mitigate them.

00:00:33.878 --> 00:00:36.286
There are techniques,
like the kinetic impacter,

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:38.163
which would impact an asteroid

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.707
to slightly change its trajectory.

00:00:41.676 --> 00:00:44.169
I've never been involved in a filming

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:46.755
where so much effort has been
made to be accurate.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.260
We want to deliver a film that's exciting and cinematic,
and blows your mind,

00:00:52.805 --> 00:00:55.972
but scientists and teachers walk out and say, 
"Hey, they got it right."

